{"name":"Leprechaun Laugh","hex":"#8cc37d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"leprechaun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of diminutive, solitary fairy or sprite, traditionally depicted as a small, bearded man wearing a green coat and hat, often found repairing a single shoe; they typically possess hidden treasure, such as a pot of gold hidden at the end of a rainbow, and can be forced to reveal its location if captured.","An Irish person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leprechaun"},{"term":"laugh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An expression of mirth particular to the human species; the sound heard in laughing; laughter.","Something that provokes mirth or scorn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To show mirth, satisfaction, or derision, by peculiar movement of the muscles of the face, particularly of the mouth, causing a lighting up of the face and eyes, and usually accompanied by the emission of explosive or chuckling sounds from the chest and throat; to indulge in laughter.","To be or appear cheerful, pleasant, mirthful, lively, or brilliant; to sparkle; to sport."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laugh"}],"entries":[{"title":"Leprechaun","blocks":[{"text":"A leprechaun is a diminutive supernatural being in Irish folklore, classed by some as a type of solitary fairy. They are usually depicted as little bearded men, wearing a coat and hat, who partake in mischief. In later times, they have been depicted as shoe-makers who have a hidden pot of gold at the end of the rainbow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Leprechaun_ill_artlibre_jnl.png/330px-Leprechaun_ill_artlibre_jnl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Leprechaun_ill_artlibre_jnl.png/500px-Leprechaun_ill_artlibre_jnl.p